Body:
@griffinmartin Thanks for the kind words and the heads-up on the Windows path!

I did some digging into the OpenCode source — it turns out it uses [`xdg-basedir`](https://github.com/sindresorhus/xdg-basedir), which resolves to `~/.local/share` on all platforms including Windows:

```js
// packages/opencode/src/global/index.ts
import { xdgData } from "xdg-basedir"
const data = path.join(xdgData!, app)
```

```js
// xdg-basedir/index.js
export const xdgData = env.XDG_DATA_HOME ||
    (homeDirectory ? path.join(homeDirectory, ".local", "share") : undefined);
```

So it looks like `~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json` should be the right path on Windows as well — I've been running it on a Windows machine with OpenCode v1.2.27 and it's been working fine so far.

That said, your plugin approach is definitely cleaner for most users — nice work on the 5-minute in-process sync! Different tradeoffs for different preferences 🙂

Instead of overwriting`~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json` just copy over the values from the exported credentials into the correct structure:

```
{
  "anthropic": {
    "type": "oauth",
    "refresh": "COPY REFRESH TOKEN HERE",
    "access": "COPY ACCESS TOKEN HERE",
    "expires": COPY EXPIRY HERE
  }
}
```
